  <text>
    <body>
      <p>In the evening, a few people continue a discussion about <rs type="keyword" ref="#religious-critique">criticism</rs>, care, and the organization of public life. The room is filled with paper and light. <rs type="person" ref="#ea-pers-001">Eleonora Gonzaga-Nevers</rs></p>
      <p>They use common words—window, table, ledger, patient, and question—and the sense stays plain. The talk remains focused on ordinary evidence and honest inquiry, with <rs type="keyword" ref="#atheism-and-science">fact</rs> guiding the exchange. <rs type="person" ref="#ea-pers-002">Baruch Spinoza</rs></p>
      <p>Nothing grand is required for a useful conclusion. <rs type="keyword" ref="#materialism">Matter</rs> and <rs type="keyword" ref="#naturalism">nature</rs> are both named before the page closes. <gap></gap></p>
    </body>
